| Version 1.1.0 |

**NEW**

- Added Hats! they can be bought from wandering traders!
- Added Cosmetic Armor slots which will allow you to wear hats and armors on top of your current gear for cosmetic purposes.
- Added Chest variants allowing you to craft different chests based on the wood type used.
- Added cute Degus mob
- Added Grappling Hooks
- Added Elytra and Tool Trims
- Added Hammers and Excavators to help out with large building projects.
- Added 11 new flowers which can be obtained through the Sniffer mob!
- Added Suspicious Dyes, which can be crafted using the Sniffer flowers and can be used to change your enchantment glint color!
- Added Albums, an Item that stores all your music discs in one and acts like a playlist for your jukeboxes! and on top of that, a portable jukebox item!
- Added Watering Can which can speed up crop growth slightly
- Added Copper Patina, which can be acquired by scraping oxidation off of copper blocks with an axe. You can use it on copper blocks to re-oxidize them, or place them down on the ground like redstone. Patina acts like redstone exactly, but it does not connect to it, so you can run wires in parallel.
- Added Rose Gold. A new and pretty tier that sits comfortably between Iron and Diamond. it's crafted using 4 Copper ingots and 4 Gold ingots and is then used to upgrade Iron into Rose Gold.
- Added 3 new food items, Sweet Berry Pie, Honeyed Apple and Fried Egg (May already be added in another form/mod)
- Added Trident Shards which can be obtained by defeating Elder Guardians in sea temples. you can craft 3 of them into a Trident!
- Added Glowsticks, a new throwable light source which can also be used underwater!
- Added Ropes! similar to terraria, they act like ladders. you can also craft rope arrows and shoot your rope!
- Added Wrench, and item that will allow you to rotate blocks!
- Added a new button in the Resourcepacks section that allows you to browse and download resourcepacks directly from within the game! (Please note that any visual bugs introduced by third party resource packs that you may have downloaded will not be handled by us.)

**CHANGES**

- Spyglass now appears in sunk ship chests.
- Powered Rails can be crafted from copper instead of gold
- Structures are now less rare and appear more frequently.
- A couple of improvements to horses. Two players can now also ride on one horse.
- Improvements to Happy Ghasts. You can now feed them different items to speed them up temporarily! you also can now reach 1 block further while riding them.
- You can now place torches, lanterns, chains, and lots more on slabs or under slabs!

- Crim

| Version 1.0.0 |

Hello!

Welcome to the opening of Everlight!

This is the message box where we will be putting our announcements and updates/changelogs. Here you can keep up to date with the latest news, announcements, and community projects and events, as well as the changelog for each version!

Everlight is a Vanilla+ pack crafted to ensure that the game stays true to Vanilla while adding enough flavors to keep things interesting.
It's specifically designed for a good and simple multiplayer experience with your friends.

Explore a new kind of world generation that stays true to Minecraft with improved visuals(Only in Default & Quality) and a good selection of new blocks and furniture blocks to spice up your builds, as well as a bunch of quality of life features added to make your experience better.
Find structures in the wild as an Explorer, or build a cozy farm with a selection of new crops as a Farmer. Build yourself a store that provides services or items as a Shopkeeper, or enjoy participating in the events to come!

Play Everlight in the way you want!
Happy launch day! Now go punch some trees.

- Renpixel, Crim & Ash
